        {
          "id": "channel_findings",
          "width": "full",
          "type": "markdown",
          "markdown": "### Channel findings (three)\n\n1. **The only loss-making channel is paid social**: `paid_social` contributed **−$4,972.75** in June at a contribution margin of **−24.04%**, the only negative one of the five channels.\n2. **The other four channels are all contribution-positive**: organic search **$6,653.11** (53.50%) > affiliates **$2,851.79** (41.40%) > email **$2,372.19** (41.15%) > paid search **$2,186.21** (26.53%).\n3. **Scale and efficiency are disconnected**: paid social took **$12,800.00 / $17,065.25 (75.0%)** of June marketing spend and **152/375 (40.5%)** of orders, pushing the five-channel total contribution profit down to **$9,090.55 (16.83%)**."
        },
